  "notes": [
    "Source: 145 .rosetta files / 763 types / 280 enums (4,226 values) / 2,699 attributes.",
    "Rosetta declares what OWL makes you infer: 0% anonymous constructs, single-parent inheritance to depth 4, explicit (lo..hi) cardinality, and an explicit scalar-vs-complex split (899 scalar attributes -> properties, 1,800 complex -> relationships).",
    "`choice` types are named unions, so DISCRIMINATOR input is declared rather than recovered from anonymous owl:unionOf. 16 choices: Asset, Payout, Product, Observable, Transfer, Instrument, Index, InterestRateIndex, Underlier and others.",
    "Choice membership is emitted as IS_<OPTION> relationships. In Rosetta an option can both extend a base type and belong to a choice (Cash extends AssetBase and is an Asset option), which is why 32 types legitimately have two parents.",
    "NOT represented: 1,290 func definitions and 615 conditions. CDM is machine-EXECUTABLE; a property graph holds its data shape, not its calculations. This is the single biggest caveat when presenting a CDM graph model.",
    "TradeState.SUCCEEDS is a derived traversal edge, not a CDM attribute -- CDM threads lifecycle through BusinessEvent (before/after TradeState). It is included because the state chain is the query most people want.",
    "Licence differs from the rest of the catalog: Community Specification License 1.0, not MIT/Apache. See NOTICE.md before redistributing derived artifacts."
  ],
